HISTCLEAN(1) ["" ["General Commands Manual"]]

# NAME

histclean - clean shell history file

# SYNOPSIS

*histclean* [options]

# DESCRIPTION

Clean duplicate shell commands from history files in-place, while
preserving the most recent unique occurrence of each command.

# OPTIONS

*-h*, *--help*
	Show help message and exit.

*-v*, *--version*
	Show version and exit.

*-d*, *--dry-run*
	Print the resulted output to stdout without modifying anything.

*-b*, *--backup*
	Create a .backup copy of the history file before modifying it.

*-w*, *--which-file*
	Print the path to the detected history file and exit.

*-i*, *--input* <FILE>
	Read history from <file> instead of the default shell
	history file (determined by $HISTFILE).

*-o*, *--output* <FILE>
	Write resulted output to the specified <file> instead of overwriting
	the input file.
	Running the command multiple times to the same *output* will overwrite
	it.

*-s*, *--shell* <SHELL>
	Override the shell type instead of auto-detecting from *$SHELL*.
	See *SUPPORTED SHELLS* below for available shells.

*-c*, *--completion* <SHELL>
	Generate completion script for the specified shell.
	See *SUPPORTED SHELLS* below for available shells.

# SUPPORTED SHELLS

* bash
* zsh

# ENVIRONMENT

*HISTFILE*
	Path to the shell history file. Must be set or provided via
	*--input*.


